###  https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlOntology#Control
:Control rdf:type owl:Class ;
         rdfs:subClassOf <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKCube#Control> ;
         <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> "Junli Liang" ,
                                                "Rob Brennan" ;
         <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-05-08"^^xsd:date ;
         <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "ISO/IEC 27002:2022(E)" ;
         rdfs:comment "An ISO control is defined as a measure that modifies or maintains risk. Some of the controls in this document are controls that modify risk, while others maintain risk. An information security policy, for example, can only maintain risk, whereas compliance with the information security policy can modify risk.  Moreover, some controls describe the same generic measure in different risk contexts. This document provides a generic mixture of organizational, people, physical and technological information security controls derived from internationally recognized best practices."@en ;
         rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://openark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKControlOntology#> ;
         rdfs:label "ISO Control"@en ;
         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An ISO control is defined as a measure that modifies or maintains risk. Some of the controls in this document are controls that modify risk, while others maintain risk. An information security policy, for example, can only maintain risk, whereas compliance with the information security policy can modify risk.  Moreover, some controls describe the same generic measure in different risk contexts. This document provides a generic mixture of organizational, people, physical and technological information security controls derived from internationally recognized best practices."@en ;
         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "ISO Control"@en .


